receipt appeared: %+v %v\", receipt, err)\n470:\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"history was evaluated by the current policy: %+v %v\", eval, err)\n475:func TestCloseoutReviewPolicyUnavailable(t *testing.T) {\n508:func TestCloseoutReviewPolicyFederation(t *testing.T) {\n535:func TestCloseoutReviewPolicyReceiptIntegrity(t *testing.T) {\n542:\treceipt, err := s.NewCloseoutReceipt(ref, *state.Review.CloseoutReview, state.Review, state.ScopeDigest, reviewFixtureNow.Add(time.Hour))\n547:\t\tforged := receipt\n550:\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"an always receipt without a required review parsed\")\n553:\tif err := s.PublishCloseoutReceipt(receipt); err != nil {\n557:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a standing receipt failed the plan: %v\", err)\n559:\tt.Run(\"a changed composition does not inherit the receipt\", func(t *testing.T) {\n562:\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a receipt carried over to another composition: %v\", err)\n566:\tt.Run(\"a corrupt receipt fails the plan as it fails closeout\", func(t *testing.T) {\n570:\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"the plan hid a corrupt receipt\")\n575:func TestCloseoutReviewPolicyInterruptedRoadmapClose(t *testing.T) {\n588:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a close interrupted before its receipt read as history: %+v %v\", eval, err)\n595:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a hand-marked roadmap read as history: %+v %v\", eval, err)\n597:\t// With evidence of the legacy closure it is history.\n605:func TestCloseoutReviewPolicyFederatedReceiptProof(t *testing.T) {\n610:\t\tt.Fatal(\"an exempt milestone without its receipt was federated as closed\")\n616:\treceipt, err := s.NewCloseoutReceipt(ref, *state.Review.CloseoutReview, state.Review, state.ScopeDigest, reviewFixtureNow.Add(time.Hour))\n620:\tif err := s.PublishCloseoutReceipt(receipt); err != nil {\n624:\tif len(blockers) != 0 || id != \"closeout-receipt:\"+ref || !strings.HasPrefix(digest, \"sha256:\") {\n625:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the receipt of an exempt close did not prove it to a consumer: %s %s %v\", id, digest, blockers)\n647:func TestCloseoutReviewPolicyStatusAloneIsNotHistory(t *testing.T) {\n64